<h2>The Production That Set the Price</h2>
<p>Two first-round picks is a quarterback or edge-rusher price, not a typical defensive tackle price. Simmons' numbers explain it. Before the trade, he led all defensive tackles with <strong>28 pressures</strong> this season, per Next Gen Stats. He was also tied for second at the position with 21 run stops, so he wasn't trading run defense for pass rush.</p>
